+## 53.3 (Tremendously Improved) AI overbuilding siege units, in particular trebuchets but not only, where they are detrimental to do build, in particular when weaker but not only anyways etc
+
+See screenshots and files about/related(ing? Anyways etc) to this issue in this [google drive folder link](https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/180Hnkhno1HgQb9rzPu-EA9ahH0dr-36K?usp=sharing).
+
+This is another nice AI enhancement :) But anyways etc. I have noticed after doing known issue as of now 53.2 that for example when continuing the game, our autoplay ai and maybe other players too produce way too many trebuchets (i had noticed the issue with cannons too before anyways etc).
+
+It is also an issue quite often mentionned by players it seems, so i'm glad i could have enhanced it but anyways etc.
+
+Before our changes, our autoplay AI has more or less 20 trebuchets and is producing one in all or if not almost all our cities which is extremely inefficient, especially considering we are not the strongest if i remember it correctly, and trebuchets are bad at anything else other than attacking cities (bad at defense, low hammer efficiency vs a catapult, cannot attack efficiently if not attacking city tiles).
+
+So i implemented a logic in `CvCityAI::AI_chooseUnit`, that i then generalized a bit less strictly for all siege units depending on era (later siege units are as of now stronger like the cannon, so give more leeway to produce some more as they can be more versatile IF AI uses them well for example for defense which shouldn't be the case yet but i didn't check for sure but in all cases i mean if i may say but anyways etc it is safer and more efficient to tell AI to not overproduce them as well even if even less strict but anyways etc), so that our offense unitai composition cannot have too many siege units in them (ranges from none to 70% of all attackers depending on various conditions, often being around 30% or similar as of now if i'm not mistaken but check code if this is updated or accurate but anyways etc).
+
+The results ingame are very good. The game took a different turn (no pun but anyways etc...) starting just before olmec was razed in the early game (for example mongol AI got an early big conquest even though was beaten down later if i may say but anyways etc), and at turn 200 instead of having useless extra trebuchets, we have a strong 16 unit stack of macemen, horse knights, etc, attacaking julius caesar AI, exactly as we wanted but anyways etc.
+
+Also, german AI seems to benefit more from these changes, as in the mid-late game he produces hussars instead (of cannons or whatever he produced then i guess but anyways etc), and secures a conquest win 50 turns sooner!! (around turn 280 instead of turn 330 before the changes), with a very impressive production and unit count with our current balance settings (that don't give per era freebies or exponential reduction to cost or such anymore if i'm not mistaken but anyways etc), with a very impressive composition at turn 285 where he wins but anyways etc of 54 hussars, 26 camel cuirassiers, 26 pikemen, 5 cannons, 25 musketmen, 26 pikemen, and a bunch of / few other units in small count anyways etc. (Another difference is also julius caesar ai was much stronger this run, securing several/many cities instead of shriking if i am not mistaken but anyways etc).
+
+Downside is we seem to underproduce siege units a bit, but this is fine, especially early, where they shouldn't be too efficient to use if not for attacking cities, so as long as we have a bit of enough should be hopefully fine, else we can tone it down (or up (in this case i mean but anyways etc)) anyways etc. Left as such for now anyways etc.
 
